-- Row il-52. EXPECTED RED: four assertions, all failing, two about each of the two defects. The count (4) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the printed words need.
-- Defect 1: the First Schedule is to carry, for two years, two items printed (18ט) and (18י) after item (18ח), and an Act adds a further item printed (18ט) after the same item from 27 January 2028
-- (the day as enacted, before any postponement). On a day when all three are read, a label names two items, so both fail. The first day of the two-year items is the Wikisource editor's reading and is
-- CONSOLIDATION-ONLY; the day chosen below, 1 March 2028, is well inside both periods on any reading of the order's start.
-- Defect 2: item (18ו) cites s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law as brought in by s 1(1) of the 2013 temporary law. The target is printed by the consolidation as lapsed (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY), and the official
-- instruments held do not give the day the period ended, so the second assertion fails with NOTHING, not with FALSE. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.

§ `Defect 1: one label names two items on one day`

-- 1. No label is borne by two items that are certainly read on the day.
#ASSERT `the labels are distinct on` (Date 1 3 2028)
-- 2. The label (18ט) names one item on the day.
#ASSERT `the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` "(18ט)" (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS 1

§ `Defect 2: the citing words need a section that the consolidation prints as lapsed`

-- 3. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`)
-- 4. The named text is in force on a day long after the period was cut; the sources held answer NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: item (18ו) to s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
